+          <h4>Identifying Concepts in Terminologies & Ontologies</h4>
+          <p> The <a href="datatypes.html#CodeableConcept">CodeableConcept</a> and <a href="datatypes.html#Coding">Coding</a> datatypes are
+            represented directly in Turtle by serializing its properties like any other FHIR element.
+            However, it's also useful to make the implicit concept references in these explicit for RDF graph querying and formal reasoning. 
+            To support these use cases, an optional <i><a href="#iri-stem">concept IRI</a></i> MAY 
+            be added to the <a href="datatypes.html#CodeableConcept">CodeableConcept</a> parent of a Coding, if this is appropriate for the meaning of the concept, using an <code>rdf:type</code> assertion or 
+            written using shorthand <b><code class="rdf" style="font-size: larger">a</code></b> in
+            Turtle.</p>
+            <p>The use of <code>rdf:type</code> also supports limited, automated testing of whether multiple Codings are properly used for a single CodeableConcept. In (uncommon) cases where the concepts referenced in a Coding are disjoint (having no intersection of extensions) -- <a href="datatypes.html#CodeableConcept">which is not allowed</a> -- an OWL reasoner will detect an inconsistency.</p>
+            <p>The following example shows concept IRIs added to an Observation.code (type CodeableConcept): </p>
+<pre class="rdf">
+&lt;http://example.org/o1&gt; a fhir:Observation ;
+  fhir:code [
+    <b>a loinc:29463-7</b>;   # OPTIONAL, but RECOMMENDED
+    <b>a sct:27113001</b>;    # OPTIONAL, but RECOMMENDED
+    fhir:coding ( [
+      fhir:system [ fhir:v "http://loinc.org" ];
+      fhir:code [ fhir:v "29463-7" ];
+      fhir:display [ fhir:v "Body Weight" ]
+    ] [
+      fhir:system [ fhir:v "http://snomed.info/sct" ];
+      fhir:code [ fhir:v "27113001" ];
+      fhir:display [ fhir:v "Body weight" ]
+    ] ) ;
+  ] ;
+</pre>
+          <p>Using the optional <a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/rdf-concept-iri">RDF Concept IRI Extension</a>, the concept IRI MAY also be attached to the Coding from which it was derived.
+            This supports cases where the concept IRI needs to be preserved in JSON or XML serialization, cases where Coding elements are used outside of CodeableConcepts, and cases where the <code>rdf:type</code> relation is not appropriate for the meaning of the concept.
+            In this example of a Questionnaire.code (type Coding), <code>fhir:l</code> is rendered to show that the concept IRI is still directly resolvable with SPARQL or OWL.
+          </p>
+<pre class="rdf">
+&lt;http://example.org/q1&gt; a fhir:Questionnaire ;
+  fhir:code ( [
+    fhir:system [ fhir:v "http://loinc.org"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
+    fhir:code [ fhir:v "100280-7" ] ;
+    fhir:extension ( [   # OPTIONAL extension
+      fhir:url [ fhir:v "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/rdf-concept-iri"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
+      fhir:value [ 
+        a fhir:Uri ;
+        fhir:v "http://loinc.org/rdf/100280-7"^^xsd:anyURI ;
+        fhir:l &lt;http://loinc.org/rdf/100280-7&gt; ;     # OPTIONAL RDF link
+      ] ;
+    ] ) ;
+  ] ) ;
+</pre>
 
